owever, since $-12\\notin N,$ we conclude that the set $A$ contains only one element, namely $n=12.$\n\nTherefore, we can write the given set as\n\n$$\nA={12}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-181767/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c2ae57a-fde8-5d07-bbff-e66fbd4428b0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181767"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-181787/selection/d602da968f855a4dc10c132bc40dad8d7a6a59db5af85bca8638397d68c46980" :answer/id #uuid "b38c8678-5a6a-5b35-ab86-b048cb702565" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{N}_{0}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181787/selection/9598736755ae5bae7a394e1db6a4b80448b26034cc5bc8e65054beaa14d3b30f" :answer/id #uuid "d9147e5a-8a14-5124-9a96-42c38beccbf4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\\pm 3,\\pm 4,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181787/selection/ea7c0fb893f7e5eec1b57d9909f8dc57ec899ce685153fe9a73c88bcfc90481b" :answer/id #uuid "a0a9c50e-7ed4-5445-b83b-1163cf1f80cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{0,\\,\\pm 2,\\,\\pm 4,\\,\\pm 6,\\,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181787/selection/d76c4df83baaf4ed610e2a8d08b314237c92b03c038e6aa58769c2709fdb9adb" :answer/id #uuid "a2d3957f-1880-5773-bce1-928cac74894c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{0,2,4,6,8,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181787/selection/7d512723ec7933fc53d818fe067378407b0cca1985b020babe9fcffa79cfd32b" :answer/id #uuid "78a150d0-1cb3-5fc1-ac94-cbb319dbc0d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181787/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e48bb30d-57b3-5780-b82c-91026f2e5a9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-181787/selection/ea7c0fb893f7e5eec1b57d9909f8dc57ec899ce685153fe9a73c88bcfc90481b" :answer-field/choices ["q-181787/selection/d602da968f855a4dc10c132bc40dad8d7a6a59db5af85bca8638397d68c46980" "q-181787/selection/9598736755ae5bae7a394e1db6a4b80448b26034cc5bc8e65054beaa14d3b30f" "q-181787/selection/ea7c0fb893f7e5eec1b57d9909f8dc57ec899ce685153fe9a73c88bcfc90481b" "q-181787/selection/d76c4df83baaf4ed610e2a8d08b314237c92b03c038e6aa58769c2709fdb9adb" "q-181787/selection/7d512723ec7933fc53d818fe067378407b0cca1985b020babe9fcffa79cfd32b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181787" :question/id #uuid "9fa8eea4-ecef-5654-b399-3872ddbe93b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-181787" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in R:\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)=1}?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)=1\n$$\n\n are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pi x & =2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =2n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,\\pm 2,\\,\\pm 4,\\,\\pm 6,\\,…\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA={0,\\,\\pm 2,\\,\\pm 4,\\,\\pm 6,\\,…}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-181787/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74611c25-8501-52a7-a705-b7e9f8f6b8ee"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181787"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-181788/selection/4ed5539c77b67cf23be9850f1282c02dba2bce0b0d606b83ca99ea1f8e625082" :answer/id #uuid "6747da73-9ddc-50bd-9f4d-b8e002542f95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\pm \\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm \\frac{3}{2},\\,\\pm \\frac{5}{2},\\,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181788/selection/203f88d94a38bb859e78e84aea518cf34952815758cf391887040455367d62ef" :answer/id #uuid "c0eb89c9-84c5-51d7-afbd-e51045df25c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "N" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181788/selection/61ef26454348ffc7d651dd4c2b6a76df435eb827281568087535bf4c7388ba00" :answer/id #uuid "b2ea2a58-f7a7-5438-a67a-267b9f820996" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{1,3,5,7,9,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181788/selection/f3a3b2d428933368a2d5f11d35a57c3ca3affae6a2503507ed920051ddc6a6a5" :answer/id #uuid "a00d5c51-016f-59a2-9fef-01990d0cb0c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{1,\\frac{1}{2},2,\\frac{3}{2},3,\\frac{5}{2},…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181788/selection/d9a6a5184ad06e63f695c86dad48eb7a5bff4041c309bd05d080bc203ebc308b" :answer/id #uuid "4121c576-624d-593a-b6ac-7841c3c4d88c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\frac{3}{2},\\,\\frac{5}{2},\\,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181788/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d8e2c9a-ae4b-5e1c-9670-38f6deef9ad5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-181788/selection/4ed5539c77b67cf23be9850f1282c02dba2bce0b0d606b83ca99ea1f8e625082" :answer-field/choices ["q-181788/selection/4ed5539c77b67cf23be9850f1282c02dba2bce0b0d606b83ca99ea1f8e625082" "q-181788/selection/203f88d94a38bb859e78e84aea518cf34952815758cf391887040455367d62ef" "q-181788/selection/61ef26454348ffc7d651dd4c2b6a76df435eb827281568087535bf4c7388ba00" "q-181788/selection/f3a3b2d428933368a2d5f11d35a57c3ca3affae6a2503507ed920051ddc6a6a5" "q-181788/selection/d9a6a5184ad06e63f695c86dad48eb7a5bff4041c309bd05d080bc203ebc308b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181788" :question/id #uuid "2abf339e-22e7-5c7c-96bd-5424e69802dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-181788" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in R:\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x)=-1}?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x)=-1\n$$\n\n are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\pi x & =\\pi +2n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =1+2n \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}+n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx=\\pm \\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm \\frac{3}{2},\\,\\pm \\frac{5}{2},\\,…\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA={\\pm \\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm \\frac{3}{2},\\,\\pm \\frac{5}{2},\\,…}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-181788/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74611c25-8501-52a7-a705-b7e9f8f6b8ee"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181788"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
